cookbook/references/native-game-semantics-use-v3-owned-buffers.md:346:The fused native lifecycle is locally checked and executes in the measured two-GPU PPO path. `engine_rs/src/training.rs` and `owl.rs.KaggricultureTrainingEnv` own the active training game batch, BigInt seed streams, typed terminal state, reward/economic/mask computation and synchronous auto-reset. It reuses the engine/decoder/encoder while dropping unused legacy native controllers from active training. The Python adapter makes one native call per step; diagnostic terminal JSON is generated lazily only when requested. Caller-owned int64 NumPy inputs remain views when contiguous, with checked Rust narrowing into scratch; strided inputs are normalized at the Python boundary. This is not a zero-copy claim for narrowing, transactional game clones or double output staging, which remain for rollback correctness.
